				\begin{document}$$\tau =\frac{K\,\lambda }{\beta \,cos\theta }$$\end{document}τ=Kλβcosθwith the shape factor K which was assumed as 0.9, the wavelength λ, the FHWM and the Bragg angle θ of the (002) peak at 2θ = 26°. For each tusk, the mean value, standard deviation and variance were determined (Supplementary Table S6).
